Smart-dispatch chunk-1 — zenanalyze-driven screenshot_lift_hint A/B
====================================================================

Date: 2026-05-18
Host: $(uname -n)
Repo: jxl-encoder (sibling workspace --entropy-mul-smart-dispatch)
Parent commit: 74b4112b (main@origin at workspace creation)
Build features: __expert butteraugli-loop parallel (release)
Effort: 7

Harness: jxl-encoder/examples/entropy_mul_smart_dispatch_ab.rs (NOT
committed to CI registry — sibling-only via temporary zenanalyze
path dep edit; the example registration in jxl-encoder/Cargo.toml is
marked LOCAL-ONLY and reverted before the commit that lands the
API + bench fixtures.)

Sweep design
------------
10 gb82-sc screenshots × 3 distances {0.5, 1.0, 2.0} × 2 modes
{smart_off, smart_on} = 60 measurements.

  smart_off : libjxl-faithful reference EntropyMulTable.
              `with_content_aware_entropy_mul(false)` (default).
  smart_on  : `with_content_aware_entropy_mul(true)` +
              `with_screenshot_lift_hint(classify_zenanalyze(rgb))`
              where the classifier rule is:

                  if palette_log2_size <= 6: Some(false)   # windows95-class
                  elif fcbr >= 0.50 && uniformity >= 0.50: Some(true)
                  else: None  # falls back to mask1x1 (W22-1)

Methodology
-----------
Per cell:
  1. Encode at distance d, effort 7.
  2. Decode with jxl-oxide in linear sRGB (CLAUDE.md jxl-oxide rule).
  3. Compute Rust butteraugli (linear) and Rust fast-ssim2 (sRGB u8).

The classifier runs once per image (Tier-1 zenanalyze sweep) and
the result is forwarded to both `smart_off` (ignored) and `smart_on`.

